THE RUN BEFORE THIS ONE WENT RED, AND THAT IS WORTH RECORDING

Run 33711437643, on the same branch one commit earlier, failed with
"creating a knowledge base answered 500". The security hardening added a
group-grant filter call to knowledge.py that passed `db`, a local the create
route deliberately does not have. The patch applied cleanly, the module parsed,
the marker counts matched and every unit assertion passed. Only this capture
went red. scripts/test_owui_skill_group_grants.py now carries a structural
guard that refuses any inserted call naming a name the enclosing function does
not bind.
